A||N||1||David Bartlett||Custom Hood, Is SMC fill needed?||||1||
Z||000000||David Bartlett||12-15-2001||03:51 PM||||I want to make a custom hood over the winter, must I use SMC repair to fill in the sides or can I use another less expensive product for this? What do you guys recommend?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bazooka||12-16-2001||10:31 PM||||David,   Fiberglas Resin and handlaid matting worked fine for me. However you should use an SMC resin or SMC panel adhesive to bond the new Fiberglas scoop to your existing SMC hood. Using SMC materials will prevent possible hairline cracks from dissimilar materials (Fiberglas to SMC). My hood is shown below. <BR> <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.members.aol.com:/m34chev/a01.jpg">  <BR>*************************************<BR>     ||||reg||1
